    "description": "At the heart of Jeddah, \"Hajeer\" tells the captivating story of a young musician and composer from the 1960s, born into a family of musicians. Suddenly struck by an illness that renders him deaf; confronted and left to fend for himself, he does not give up. With authentic and deeply complex characters, this story addresses universal themes such as love, hope, resilience, and the struggle against prejudice, offering a unique perspective on life’s challenges. In this poignant drama of love and despair, Hajeer, revitalized by newfound strength, confronts the betrayal of his beloved Aalya and asserts his rights. Through his struggle, Hajeer composes a symphony of redemption, revealing the enduring imprint of eternal love.",
